cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Zhinao Xiandao: a PYNQ-Z2 terminal for stroke severity prediction"
abstract: >-
  A research prototype that runs a 62-input clinical DNN on a PYNQ-Z2 (Zynq-7020).
  The network is factorised into a low-rank form (62-500-4-500-64-500-1) and
  implemented as a 16-bit fixed-point HLS kernel with on-chip resident weights,
  reaching 1.42-1.58 ms per sample end-to-end from the processing system.
  It includes a Flask UI on the ARM core, a four-permutation approximate
  Shapley explainer (252 model evaluations), a touch terminal, and an OV5640
  single-frame capture path. Not a medical device.
authors:
  - name: "Zhinao Xiandao Project Team"
    affiliation: "FPGA Innovation Competition (6组-智脑先导)"
